    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of the change (release version 2 of the owner identity):\n\n## New single source of truth\n**`IdentityVersion`** (model) \u2014 holds `NUMBER = 2` (the api/audit-schema version), `TAG = \"V2\"`, and the version\u20112 region\u2011code algorithm: `regionCode(region)` mixes the tag in (`\"NSW\"` \u2192 `\"V2NSW\"`), `plainRegion(code)` strips it back out. This is reused everywhere so the \"2\"/\"V2\" literal lives in exactly one place.\n\n## Identifiers rederived under V2 (each changes; no V1 value recurs)\n- **memberId** \u2014 `MemberIdAssigner` now builds the id from `IdentityVersion.regionCode(owner.getRegion())`, so the `REGION` segment (and its Luhn digit) become version\u20112, e.g. `V2NSW261A2B3C4D9`.\n- **identityKey** \u2014 `Owner.getIdentityKey()` mixes the `V2` tag into the hashed input, preserving the \"equal keys \u21d2 duplicate\" rule for the duplicate checker.\n- **householdId** \u2014 `HouseholdMatcher.householdId()` mixes the `V2` tag into the hashed key, preserving same\u2011household resolution (household *matching* is unaffected \u2014 it keys off the raw fields, not the hash).\n\n## Tag stays inside identifiers only\n`Owner.getLocality()` reads the region out of the member id and strips the `V2` tag via `plainRegion`, so it stays plain (`NSW`). `timezone` and the owner segment's area derive from that plain locality \u2014 verified by the audit output showing `STANDARD_METRO`.\n\n## Response shape\nOpenAPI `Owner` schema now nests `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` under a new **`OwnerIdentity`** object and adds a top\u2011level integer **`apiVersion: 2`**; the three flat fields are gone. `OwnerMapper` populates `identity.*` and sets `apiVersion` from `IdentityVersion.NUMBER`.\n\n## Audit event \u2192 schema v2\n`OwnerCreatedEvent` adds **`schemaVersion: 2`** and carries the **owner segment recomputed from the version\u20112 identity**. Serialized output: `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,...,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
