    "probe_text": "`POST /api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:190`), reached with base path `/api` + operation path `/owners`. Here is everything applied, in execution order.\n\n## Precondition\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`: the caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the request is rejected before anything runs.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean-validation pass (`@Valid` on the body, via `@InitBinder`)\nThe body is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, and `initOwnerFieldsBinder` (`:160`) registers two validators that run **before** the method body. These both **validate and mutate** the DTO. If either records an error, the request fails as a 400 and no side-effects below occur.\n\n`OwnerFieldsValidator` runs first, in this internal order:\n1. **Address normalization + presence** \u2014 prefers the structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (normalizes them, writes them back, composes them into `address`); otherwise normalizes the flat `address`. An address is required in one form or the other (else field error on `address`).\n2. **Required non-blank text fields** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` must be present and non-blank.\n3. **Telephone canonicalization** \u2014 only if `telephone` had no prior error: normalized to E.164 form and written back; rejected if not a valid number.\n4. **Email (optional)** \u2014 if present, must be syntactically valid, must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist, and is normalized to lower case (written back).\n5. **Postcode (optional)** \u2014 if present, must be a valid 4-digit code for the owner's `city`.\n\n`RegistrationDateValidator` runs second:\n6. **Registration date not in the future** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` is supplied, it must not be after the server's current date.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Method body (`addOwner`)\n7. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header is present and already seen, the previously created owner is re-read and returned (`200 OK`), skipping all steps below.\n8. **Map** DTO \u2192 `Owner` (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n9. **Registration date assignment** (`registrationDateAssigner`) \u2014 sets the effective date: the supplied date, or today if none; then rolls any weekend/holiday forward to the next business day.\n10. **City-capacity gate** (`cityCapacityChecker.isCityAtCapacity`) \u2014 throws `CityAtCapacityException` if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners.\n11. **Capacity warning flag** (`cityCapacityChecker.assignCapacityWarning`) \u2014 sets `capacityWarning = true` when the city holds 40\u201349 owners.\n12. **Daily-limit gate** (`dailyRegistrationLimiter.isDailyLimitReached`) \u2014 throws `DailyRegistrationLimitException` if \u2265 100 owners already carry that effective registration date.\n13. **Household id** (`householdAssigner.assign`) \u2014 sets `householdId`, derived deterministically from last name + postcode.\n14. **Identity-duplicate gate** (`identityDuplicateChecker.isDuplicate`) \u2014 throws `DuplicateOwnerException` if a non-deleted existing owner shares the same identity key (hash of telephone, email, last-name Soundex).\n15. **Capture** `declaredHouseholdMember` = whether `sharesHousehold` is `TRUE` (used in step 20).\n16. **Household size** (`householdSizeAssigner.assign`) \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing the `householdId`, plus one.\n17. **Member id** (`memberIdAssigner.assign`) \u2014 sets `memberId` from region + fiscal year + telephone/last-name hash, de-duplicated against existing member ids.\n18. **Namesake count** (`namesakeCounter.assign`) \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n19. **Membership level** (`membershipLevelAssigner.assign`) \u2014 sets `membershipPoints` and the banded `membershipLevel`, capped at one above the highest level in the household.\n20. **Bulk-signup warning** (`bulkSignupWarningAssigner.assign`) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > 80 owners already share the registration date.\n21. **Possible-duplicate flags** (`possibleDuplicateAssigner.assign`) \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` from a soft match; a declared household member is never flagged.\n22. **Persist** (`clinicService.saveOwner`) \u2014 saves the owner (assigns its id).\n23. **Remember idempotency key** \u2014 if a key was supplied, `idempotentOwnerStore.remember` stores the new owner's id under it.\n24. **Audit log** (`ownerCreationAuditLogger.logCreated`) \u2014 writes a human-readable `AUDIT` line and a serialized JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent`.\n25. **Welcome notification** (`welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome`) \u2014 writes a `NOTIFY` log line.\n26. **Response** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, sets the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, returns `201 CREATED`.\n\nNote the ordering constraints baked in: capacity/limit checks (steps 10, 12, 20) and the count-based assigners (16, 18) all run **before** the save so the new owner doesn't count itself; and `membershipLevelAssigner` (19) depends on `namesakeCount` and `householdSize` being set first (16, 18)."
